    'tag. You already know how to check a tag and how to change a value that lives in the class ' +
    'body. What is genuinely new is who moves the Player — and until that changes, a solid spike ' +
    'is a picture you can stand inside.',
  sizeTest:
    'The test: does the part name the thing that does the work? "Take damage" is an effect, not a ' +
    'part. "Hand the movement to the physics engine" is a part — and it is the only one here that ' +
    'changes what your character is allowed to do.',
  turns: [
    'Your coin count only ever goes up, so it needs no rule at all. Health only goes down, and it has a floor. Which part above keeps health inside the range where the number still means something — and what would the Console print on a second spike without it?',
